<abstract><p>The study compares connector retention under repeated insertion and documents the observed limits. It does not claim that every battery assembly uses the same connector or replacement process.</p></abstract></article-meta></front>
<body><sec id="methods"><title>Measured procedure</title>
<p>Disconnect power before removing the battery, record the connector orientation, and retain the original screws. We measured a retention force of 12 N after twenty cycles and compared it with the published service requirements <xref ref-type="bibr" rid="ref1 ref2">1,2</xref>.</p>
<list list-type="order"><list-item><p>Record the exact model.</p></list-item><list-item><p>Inspect the connector.</p></list-item></list>
<p>Relative capacity was calculated as <inline-formula><mml:math><mml:mfrac><mml:mi>C</mml:mi><mml:mi>C0</mml:mi></mml:mfrac></mml:math></inline-formula>. A separate notation was <inline-formula><alternatives><tex-math><![CDATA[x^2 + y^2]]></tex-math><mml:math><mml:mi>duplicate-equation</mml:mi></mml:math></alternatives></inline-formula>.</p>
